{"ts": "2026-10-27T12:43:12.239652Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T1230Z-07f9", "unit": "openspec:add-fake-oidc", "seq": 75, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-003", "id": "Q-003", "status": "answered", "reason": "Verified in the file: AUTH_PATH already starts with /realms/ursitoare, and lines 45 and 88 prefix it with fake.issuer, which the spec (Default start) and server.test.ts:168 define as url + \"/realms/ursitoare\", so the request path doubles the realm segment. The spec places the endpoint at /realms/ursitoare/protocol/openid-connect/auth and the design says the form action is the request path plus raw query; line 100 asserts the action equals AUTH_PATH plus the query, so no handler can satisfy both the doubled request path and the single-realm action. The question comes from the implementer during the red step, not a fix task, and the harness note allows an answer naming the file to unfreeze it, as Q-002 did for the same pattern. The clarifier suggestion is the minimal correct change.", "called": true, "tasks": ["2.2"], "target": null, "kind": "technical", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 0.7815682500000001, "decision": "accept", "answer_sha256": "ff79f000430ec0769835d36a2172634ff95b8b89c934cdcd05032e8e61af43ed", "checked": [{"ref": "test/support/fake-oidc/authorize.test.ts:9", "quote": "const AUTH_PATH = \"/realms/ursitoare/protocol/openid-connect/auth\";", "claim": "AUTH_PATH already contains the realm prefix."}, {"ref": "test/support/fake-oidc/authorize.test.ts:45", "quote": "return `${fake.issuer}${AUTH_PATH}?${queryOf(params)}`;", "claim": "authUrl prefixes the realm-bearing path with the issuer, doubling /realms/ursitoare."}, {"ref": "test/support/fake-oidc/authorize.test.ts:88", "quote": "const response = await fetch(`${fake.issuer}${AUTH_PATH}?${query}`, {", "claim": "The GET form test builds the same doubled path."}, {"ref": "test/support/fake-oidc/authorize.test.ts:100", "quote": "const action = escapeQuery(`${AUTH_PATH}?${query}`);", "claim": "The action assertion expects the single-realm path, contradicting the doubled request path."}, {"ref": "test/support/fake-oidc/server.test.ts:168", "quote": "assert.equal(fake.issuer, `${fake.url}/realms/ursitoare`);", "claim": "The issuer is the server url plus /realms/ursitoare, so fake.url is the correct origin for a full path."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/test-fake-oidc/spec.md#scenario-default-start", "quote": "`issuer` equals `url + \"/realms/ursitoare\"`", "claim": "The spec fixes the issuer as url plus the realm path."}, {"ref": "spec:specs/test-fake-oidc/spec.md#requirement-the-authorization-endpoint-validates-the-request-and-issues-a-one-use-code", "quote": "The endpoint at `/realms/ursitoare/protocol/openid-connect/auth` SHALL check `client_id`", "claim": "The spec places the auth endpoint at the single-realm path, so requests must go to url plus AUTH_PATH."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md", "quote": "`GET` renders the form; its `action` is the path plus the raw query.", "claim": "The design makes the form action equal the request path, so the request path must equal AUTH_PATH as line 100 expects."}]}
